    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard \u2014 metrics, sources & caveats",
      "datasource": null,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 11
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## InfluxDB Buckets \u2014 storage, records & throughput\n\nPer-bucket inventory of the home InfluxDB instance, sampled every 5 min by the\n`influxdb/bucket-stats` collector and stored in the `ops` bucket\n(`bucket_stats` measurement).\n\n| Metric | Meaning | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Storage** | On-disk size = compacted TSM files + WAL/cache | `storage_tsm_files_disk_bytes` + `storage_cache_disk_bytes` |\n| **Series** | Series *cardinality* (distinct tag-sets), **not** row count | `storage_bucket_series_num` |\n| **Measurements** | Distinct measurements in the bucket | `storage_bucket_measurement_num` |\n| **Throughput** | Points written per second, per bucket | counted via Flux over the trailing 5-min window |\n\n**Why throughput is derived:** InfluxDB's `/metrics` only exposes write counts\n*globally* (`storage_writer_ok_points`), never per bucket \u2014 so the collector\ncounts each bucket's points over the trailing window and divides. Internal\n`_monitoring` / `_tasks` buckets are excluded.\n\n**References:** collector `influxdb/bucket-stats/README.md` \u00b7 layout from\n[issue #74](https://github.com/tommyroar/observability-config/issues/74) \u00b7 raw metrics at `http://localhost:8086/metrics`.\n"
      }
    }
